{
  "_about": "Items Link can't hold up as they are, and how the randomizer still holds them up (tools/progressive.py HOLD_*; read back by tools/rando/no_pose_check.py). Link's item-get pose ends when the shown item's AS plays Rotate_GetDemo (Dm_SY_GetInEvent Item_Position Event51: Player_Event.EventIgnitionShowItem {IsAsPlay: True, IsWaitEnd: True, ASCommand: Rotate_GetDemo}); an actor whose AS (its ActorParam's ASRef: AS/Item_Common.root.asb for 223 vanilla actors) lacks that command, or that has no AS at all, is never let go: the game freezes (NX2-ZOOTR in game: the Fairy Ocarina gift, the small seed bag from a scrub, the small stick bag). These 26 are every such actor the item map and progressive tiers can give (scan of all 8,373 actor packs). Chests don't freeze on them: their own item display (Dm_SY_TreasureboxSmall ItemDisplay Event34, Dm_SY_Treasurebox Item_Rotation Event111) plays the command without waiting.",
  "own": {
    "_about": "The actor itself gets the hold-up animation, as every holdable item has it: ASInfoRef Component/ASInfo/Item_GetDemo (no auto-play), ASRef AS/Item_Common.root.asb, AnimationRef the AnimationParam of 'anim_from' (Item_Common_Animation plus the model's own), files copied byte for byte from those packs; its ActorInfo heaps raised to 'heap_from''s. NX2-ZOOTR did this to the songs (with Sheik's harp model) and saw them spin above Link in game. Only actors no vanilla scene animates: the songs and small bags are never shown in vanilla. The songs' model: the Triforce work's note model when parity/_show_models.py has one (keyed by the song's 'model_key'; tools/progressive.py song_model_ops puts it on the song actor itself, so chests, ground looks and the hold-up all show it), else the song's own (Obj_Rupee).",
