  "show": {
    "_about": "Items Link can't hold up as they are because vanilla scenes animate them (stones and medallions in their get cutscenes, the ocarinas as the instrument Link plays, the Master Sword as the equipped weapon): they stay untouched, and the hold-up creates a display actor of our own with the same model (\"displays\") while the window, the pouch add, the fanfare and the get glow name the item itself (Dm_SY_GetInEvent:Rando_GetShown). Vanilla shows a display-only actor the same way (MiniGame_Fishing_Sub: Item_Hat_FishingPondOwner). Don't use the quest/pouch menu's 3D items (*_ImportantMenu, Pouch_Ocarina_*: Pouch_Item_Base menu actors with no item-get event AI) or, for the Master Sword, the unused 38-character actor. I tried them in game (test_guardroom): the Ocarina's hold-up crashed, the Kokiri Emerald's showed nothing and the long name was never created (the show-item create keeps 31 characters), so the ignition read an empty ShowItem slot (OneShotShowItemInvalidateShadow, fn 0x82963040, a null read at +0x270).",
    "Item_Stone_Forest": "Rando_Show_StoneForest",
    "Item_Stone_Fire": "Rando_Show_StoneFire",
    "Item_Stone_Water": "Rando_Show_StoneWater",
    "Item_Medal_Light": "Rando_Show_MedalLight",
    "Item_Medal_Forest": "Rando_Show_MedalForest",
