  "displays": {
    "_about": "Display actors the randomizer builds (tools/progressive.py display_ops; built when any part of a plan names them). Each is a NEW actor type: a pack copied from BASE_PACK (Item_Medal_Light's: Item_EventObject_Base, the item-get event AI PouchContent.event.root, a key item's pouch parameters, no physics), the hold-up animation set every holdable item has (ASRef AS/Item_Common.root.asb with Rotate_GetDemo, ASInfo Item_GetDemo, an AnimationParam naming Item_Common_Animation: 'anim_from''s, byte copies), the model of 'model_from' (its ModelInfo, byte copy; or parity/_show_models.py's model for this display when it has one), and new ActorInfo/GameActorInfo rows (add_row: a copy of BASE_ROW's with the model's names and bounds, the animation resources, 'for' as ActorName and the largest heaps of the rows involved). Names stay within 25 characters (the show-item create keeps 31; OotrR #3 crashed over 25); a brand-new short-named type is proven on Longshot (the Triforce work's Rando_ProbeTriforce). 'look_for': the pickup actors and OoTR item-name prefixes whose ground look (tools/rando/drops.py item_display) is this display. A display with no 'model_from' exists only once _show_models.py gives it a model. The Rando_Show_Soul* displays: the souls' figures, held up by extras_souls' give entries and shown as the souls' ground looks: each boss soul's is the Hall of Fallen Foes figure of its enemy with the enemy's own materials and textures (parity/_soul_figures.py: a smaller copy of the boss's model, the museum's pose baked in; the display takes the museum actor's heaps), the bean soul's the magic bean itself (Item_MagicBean's own model and animation set).",
